1
00:00:00,182 --> 00:00:05,575
Probability questions on the SAT
are almost never about hard math.

2
00:00:05,647 --> 00:00:09,519
They come down to one decision:
what do you divide by?

3
00:00:09,539 --> 00:00:12,467
Get the total right, and
the rest is a fraction.

4
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:16,802
The common mistake is dividing by the
grand total when the question has quietly

5
00:00:16,822 --> 00:00:18,286
narrowed the group.

6
00:00:18,715 --> 00:00:24,444
One phrase, like given that, or if a
customer who chose popcorn is selected,

7
00:00:24,464 --> 00:00:26,036
changes the denominator.

8
00:00:26,215 --> 00:00:29,679
And the trap answer is waiting
for anyone who misses it.

9
00:00:29,741 --> 00:00:33,650
In this lesson: basic probability,
reading two-way tables,

10
00:00:33,670 --> 00:00:36,685
conditional probability, and versus or,

11
00:00:36,705 --> 00:00:39,527
complements, and expected counts.

12
00:00:39,633 --> 00:00:42,560
Seven practice questions, easy to hard.

13
00:00:42,580 --> 00:00:46,095
Probability is favorable
outcomes over total outcomes,

14
00:00:46,115 --> 00:00:48,631
when every outcome is equally likely.

15
00:00:48,651 --> 00:00:51,203
It's always between zero and one.

16
00:00:51,223 --> 00:00:54,473
Zero means impossible,
and one means certain.

17
00:00:54,512 --> 00:00:56,512
The complement is everything else.

18
00:00:56,547 --> 00:01:01,350
The probability that something does not
happen is one minus the probability that

19
00:01:01,370 --> 00:01:02,206
it does.

20
00:01:02,226 --> 00:01:04,456
If the chance of rain is three tenths,

21
00:01:04,476 --> 00:01:07,326
the chance of no rain is seven tenths.

22
00:01:07,346 --> 00:01:08,346
Question one.

23
00:01:08,382 --> 00:01:11,898
A box contains six red
tiles, nine blue tiles,

24
00:01:11,918 --> 00:01:13,560
and five green tiles.

25
00:01:13,632 --> 00:01:15,932
One tile is selected at random.

26
00:01:15,952 --> 00:01:19,774
What is the probability that
the selected tile is not blue?

27
00:01:19,831 --> 00:01:21,045
Pause and try it.

28
00:01:24,226 --> 00:01:28,992
Total tiles: six plus
nine plus five is twenty.

29
00:01:29,012 --> 00:01:33,491
Not blue means red or green,
and six plus five is eleven.

30
00:01:33,511 --> 00:01:36,262
So the probability is eleven twentieths.

31
00:01:36,691 --> 00:01:40,278
Or use the complement:
one minus nine twentieths.

32
00:01:40,298 --> 00:01:41,206
Same answer.

33
00:01:41,226 --> 00:01:42,834
The answer is B.

34
00:01:42,883 --> 00:01:45,848
Nine twentieths is the
probability of blue.

35
00:01:46,026 --> 00:01:50,077
Nine elevenths and eleven ninths
compare one group to the other group.

36
00:01:50,097 --> 00:01:52,506
That's a ratio, not a probability.

37
00:01:52,526 --> 00:01:54,541
And eleven ninths is bigger than one,

38
00:01:54,561 --> 00:01:56,811
so it can't be a probability at all.

39
00:01:56,864 --> 00:02:00,307
Many SAT probability
questions use a two-way table.

40
00:02:00,327 --> 00:02:03,344
It sorts one group by
two categories at once:

41
00:02:03,364 --> 00:02:06,629
one category across the
rows, one down the columns,

42
00:02:06,649 --> 00:02:08,506
with totals on the edges.

43
00:02:08,543 --> 00:02:10,809
Here's the table for
the next four questions.

44
00:02:10,829 --> 00:02:12,722
The numbers are made up for practice.

45
00:02:12,757 --> 00:02:15,845
A movie theater surveyed
two hundred forty customers.

46
00:02:15,865 --> 00:02:19,023
Each row is the show
time, matinee or evening.

47
00:02:19,043 --> 00:02:21,809
Each column is the snack: popcorn, candy,

48
00:02:21,829 --> 00:02:22,745
or nothing.

49
00:02:22,765 --> 00:02:25,173
Matinee: forty-eight
popcorn, twenty-two candy,

50
00:02:25,193 --> 00:02:28,194
thirty nothing, for a
total of one hundred.

51
00:02:28,444 --> 00:02:31,816
Evening: eighty-four
popcorn, thirty-six candy,

52
00:02:31,836 --> 00:02:35,102
twenty nothing, for a
total of one hundred forty.

53
00:02:35,122 --> 00:02:37,872
The column totals are
one hundred thirty-two,

54
00:02:37,908 --> 00:02:39,722
fifty-eight, and fifty.

55
00:02:39,742 --> 00:02:41,864
Before any question, find the totals.

56
00:02:41,884 --> 00:02:46,222
Each row total, each column total,
and the grand total in the corner.

57
00:02:46,242 --> 00:02:48,043
Those are your possible denominators.

58
00:02:48,063 --> 00:02:50,170
The question tells you which one to use.

59
00:02:50,251 --> 00:02:51,680
Here's the key idea.

60
00:02:51,930 --> 00:02:56,930
Take one cell: the thirty matinee
customers who chose nothing.

61
00:02:57,037 --> 00:02:59,767
That one number can turn into
three different probabilities,

62
00:02:59,787 --> 00:03:01,537
depending on the denominator.

63
00:03:01,557 --> 00:03:06,144
Out of all customers, thirty over
two hundred forty is one eighth:

64
00:03:06,164 --> 00:03:08,109
matinee and nothing.

65
00:03:08,129 --> 00:03:12,109
Out of the matinee row, thirty
over one hundred is three tenths:

66
00:03:12,129 --> 00:03:13,914
nothing, given matinee.

67
00:03:14,128 --> 00:03:18,109
Out of the nothing column, thirty
over fifty is three fifths:

68
00:03:18,129 --> 00:03:20,409
matinee, given nothing.

69
00:03:20,429 --> 00:03:22,158
Given means you restrict the group.

70
00:03:22,178 --> 00:03:27,143
Stop looking at the whole table, and
look only at one row or one column.

71
00:03:27,179 --> 00:03:30,429
That row or column total
becomes the denominator.

72
00:03:30,489 --> 00:03:33,540
The SAT words it in different ways.

73
00:03:33,560 --> 00:03:35,040
Given that.

74
00:03:35,060 --> 00:03:36,148
Of the customers who.

75
00:03:36,168 --> 00:03:39,825
Or, if a customer who
chose popcorn is selected.

76
00:03:39,845 --> 00:03:42,540
They all mean the same
thing: restrict first,

77
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:43,667
then count.

78
00:03:43,746 --> 00:03:44,996
Question two.

79
00:03:45,175 --> 00:03:49,405
Using the table, if one of these
customers is selected at random,

80
00:03:49,425 --> 00:03:53,975
what is the probability that the customer
attended an evening show and chose

81
00:03:53,995 --> 00:03:54,784
candy?

82
00:03:54,804 --> 00:03:56,019
Pause and try it.

83
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:00,394
There's no condition here.

84
00:04:00,414 --> 00:04:02,430
The customer is chosen from everyone,

85
00:04:02,450 --> 00:04:04,751
so the denominator is the grand total,

86
00:04:04,771 --> 00:04:06,001
two hundred forty.

87
00:04:06,021 --> 00:04:09,072
Evening and candy is one cell: thirty-six.

88
00:04:09,092 --> 00:04:12,001
Thirty-six over two hundred
forty is three twentieths.

89
00:04:12,021 --> 00:04:13,700
The answer is A.

90
00:04:13,747 --> 00:04:16,870
Nine thirty-fifths divides
by the evening row.

91
00:04:16,890 --> 00:04:19,906
Eighteen twenty-ninths
divides by the candy column.

92
00:04:19,926 --> 00:04:23,012
Both answer a given
question that wasn't asked.

93
00:04:23,032 --> 00:04:26,817
And seven twelfths is just
the chance of an evening show.

94
00:04:26,837 --> 00:04:27,924
Question three.

95
00:04:27,944 --> 00:04:31,603
If a customer who chose
popcorn is selected at random,

96
00:04:31,623 --> 00:04:34,515
what is the probability that
the customer attended a matinee?

97
00:04:35,319 --> 00:04:36,533
Pause and try it.

98
00:04:39,714 --> 00:04:41,836
Who chose popcorn is the condition.

99
00:04:41,856 --> 00:04:43,480
Restrict to the popcorn column.

100
00:04:43,500 --> 00:04:45,730
There are one hundred
thirty-two customers in it,

101
00:04:45,750 --> 00:04:48,730
and forty-eight of them
attended a matinee.

102
00:04:48,750 --> 00:04:52,622
Forty-eight over one hundred
thirty-two reduces to four elevenths.

103
00:04:52,642 --> 00:04:54,143
The answer is B.

104
00:04:54,171 --> 00:04:56,436
Twelve twenty-fifths is
the reverse question:

105
00:04:56,456 --> 00:04:58,293
popcorn, given matinee.

106
00:04:58,313 --> 00:05:00,365
Same cell, wrong total.

107
00:05:00,385 --> 00:05:02,421
One fifth uses the grand total.

108
00:05:02,456 --> 00:05:05,793
Mixing up the row and the column
is an easy mistake to make,

109
00:05:05,813 --> 00:05:09,635
so highlight the condition's row
or column before you calculate.

110
00:05:09,692 --> 00:05:10,743
Question four.

111
00:05:10,763 --> 00:05:13,799
If one of these customers
is selected at random,

112
00:05:13,870 --> 00:05:18,620
what is the probability that the customer
attended a matinee or chose popcorn?

113
00:05:18,661 --> 00:05:19,876
Pause and try it.

114
00:05:24,057 --> 00:05:25,985
Or means either one, or both.

115
00:05:26,307 --> 00:05:30,680
The tempting move is to add the
matinee total and the popcorn total,

116
00:05:30,700 --> 00:05:32,485
one hundred plus one hundred thirty-two.

117
00:05:32,663 --> 00:05:36,557
But the forty-eight customers
who did both get counted twice.

118
00:05:36,636 --> 00:05:38,259
Count each person once.

119
00:05:38,279 --> 00:05:40,866
Take the whole matinee row, one hundred.

120
00:05:40,886 --> 00:05:43,866
Then add the popcorn customers
who aren't already in it:

121
00:05:43,886 --> 00:05:46,116
the evening popcorn cell, eighty-four.

122
00:05:46,136 --> 00:05:48,616
That's one hundred eighty-four
out of two hundred forty,

123
00:05:48,636 --> 00:05:51,136
which reduces to twenty-three thirtieths.

124
00:05:51,196 --> 00:05:52,998
The formula says the same thing.

125
00:05:53,018 --> 00:05:56,676
The probability of A or B
is the probability of A,

126
00:05:56,696 --> 00:06:00,731
plus the probability of B,
minus the probability of both.

127
00:06:00,910 --> 00:06:03,105
One hundred plus one hundred thirty-two,

128
00:06:03,125 --> 00:06:06,018
minus forty-eight, is
one hundred eighty-four.

129
00:06:06,116 --> 00:06:09,937
If you got twenty-nine thirtieths,
you counted the overlap twice.

130
00:06:09,957 --> 00:06:11,866
Probabilities also predict counts.

131
00:06:11,886 --> 00:06:15,258
Expected count equals
probability times the total.

132
00:06:15,278 --> 00:06:20,151
If a coin lands heads half the time, in
two hundred flips you'd expect about one

133
00:06:20,171 --> 00:06:21,206
hundred heads.

134
00:06:21,289 --> 00:06:22,090
Question five.

135
00:06:22,110 --> 00:06:26,554
The theater expects three thousand six
hundred evening customers next month.

136
00:06:26,574 --> 00:06:30,947
If the proportion of evening customers
who choose popcorn is the same as in the

137
00:06:30,967 --> 00:06:35,626
survey, how many of next month's evening
customers would be expected to choose

138
00:06:35,646 --> 00:06:36,547
popcorn?

139
00:06:36,567 --> 00:06:37,781
Pause and try it.

140
00:06:41,963 --> 00:06:44,193
The new group is evening customers only,

141
00:06:44,213 --> 00:06:46,121
so use the evening row.

142
00:06:46,141 --> 00:06:50,120
Eighty-four of the one hundred forty
evening customers chose popcorn.

143
00:06:50,140 --> 00:06:51,478
That's three fifths.

144
00:06:51,498 --> 00:06:55,906
Three fifths of three thousand six
hundred is two thousand one hundred sixty.

145
00:06:55,926 --> 00:06:57,737
The answer is D.

146
00:06:57,757 --> 00:07:00,078
Each wrong choice uses the wrong rate.

147
00:07:00,256 --> 00:07:04,094
One thousand nine hundred eighty
uses popcorn out of all customers.

148
00:07:04,114 --> 00:07:07,130
One thousand two hundred sixty
divides by the grand total.

149
00:07:07,150 --> 00:07:10,872
And one thousand seven hundred
twenty-eight uses the matinee row.

150
00:07:10,892 --> 00:07:13,193
Sometimes the SAT flips the question.

151
00:07:13,213 --> 00:07:16,321
It gives you the probability
and asks for a missing count.

152
00:07:16,392 --> 00:07:19,908
Write favorable over total, set
it equal to the probability,

153
00:07:19,928 --> 00:07:20,891
and solve.

154
00:07:20,911 --> 00:07:22,268
Question six.

155
00:07:22,554 --> 00:07:26,554
A jar contains only red
marbles and blue marbles.

156
00:07:26,626 --> 00:07:29,876
There are twelve red marbles in the jar.

157
00:07:30,018 --> 00:07:35,034
If one marble is selected at random,
the probability that it is red is three

158
00:07:35,054 --> 00:07:35,963
eighths.

159
00:07:35,983 --> 00:07:38,766
How many blue marbles are in the jar?

160
00:07:38,786 --> 00:07:40,000
Pause and try it.

161
00:07:43,182 --> 00:07:45,732
Red over total equals three eighths.

162
00:07:45,752 --> 00:07:49,197
So twelve over the total
equals three over eight.

163
00:07:49,217 --> 00:07:52,661
Cross multiply: three times
the total is ninety-six,

164
00:07:52,681 --> 00:07:55,609
so the total is thirty-two marbles.

165
00:07:55,641 --> 00:07:57,855
But the question asks for blue marbles.

166
00:07:58,140 --> 00:08:00,478
Thirty-two minus twelve is twenty.

167
00:08:00,498 --> 00:08:02,033
Enter twenty.

168
00:08:02,069 --> 00:08:03,549
Thirty-two is the trap.

169
00:08:03,569 --> 00:08:06,068
It's the total, not the blue count.

170
00:08:06,125 --> 00:08:08,232
Question seven, the hardest one.

171
00:08:08,267 --> 00:08:12,498
At a high school, sixty percent of the
students take Spanish and the other forty

172
00:08:12,518 --> 00:08:14,319
percent take French.

173
00:08:14,339 --> 00:08:16,303
No student takes both.

174
00:08:16,482 --> 00:08:20,839
Of the students who take Spanish,
twenty-five percent are in the band.

175
00:08:21,196 --> 00:08:25,375
Of the students who take French,
forty-five percent are in the band.

176
00:08:25,424 --> 00:08:29,083
If a student who is in the
band is selected at random,

177
00:08:29,103 --> 00:08:32,138
what is the probability that
the student takes French?

178
00:08:32,158 --> 00:08:33,210
Pause and try it.

179
00:08:33,230 --> 00:08:34,801
Take a little longer on this one.

180
00:08:38,985 --> 00:08:40,715
There's no table, so build one.

181
00:08:40,735 --> 00:08:42,858
Pretend the school has
one hundred students.

182
00:08:42,878 --> 00:08:46,393
Then sixty take Spanish
and forty take French.

183
00:08:46,413 --> 00:08:51,143
Twenty-five percent of sixty is
fifteen Spanish students in the band.

184
00:08:51,163 --> 00:08:55,700
Forty-five percent of forty is
eighteen French students in the band.

185
00:08:55,760 --> 00:08:57,225
Now read the condition.

186
00:08:57,795 --> 00:09:02,705
A student in the band is selected, so
the denominator is everyone in the band:

187
00:09:02,725 --> 00:09:05,062
fifteen plus eighteen, or thirty-three.

188
00:09:05,082 --> 00:09:07,812
Eighteen of them take French.

189
00:09:07,832 --> 00:09:10,705
Eighteen over thirty-three
is six elevenths.

190
00:09:10,725 --> 00:09:12,546
The answer is D.

191
00:09:12,617 --> 00:09:14,010
Look at the traps.

192
00:09:14,046 --> 00:09:16,312
Nine twentieths is the reverse condition:

193
00:09:16,332 --> 00:09:17,669
band, given French.

194
00:09:17,689 --> 00:09:21,562
Thirty-three hundredths is the chance
a student is in the band at all.

195
00:09:21,582 --> 00:09:24,204
And nine fiftieths is French and band,

196
00:09:24,224 --> 00:09:25,062
out of everyone.

197
00:09:25,082 --> 00:09:28,347
Picking one hundred works for
any percent question like this,

198
00:09:28,367 --> 00:09:30,046
because the total cancels.

199
00:09:30,114 --> 00:09:31,522
Here's the test-day method.

200
00:09:31,542 --> 00:09:33,557
Step one: find the condition.

201
00:09:33,577 --> 00:09:37,165
Look for given, of the, among, or who.

202
00:09:37,185 --> 00:09:38,129
Underline it.

203
00:09:38,149 --> 00:09:41,185
If there's no condition,
the group is everyone.

204
00:09:41,239 --> 00:09:45,183
Step two: highlight the row or
column the condition points to.

205
00:09:45,203 --> 00:09:47,254
That total is your denominator.

206
00:09:47,274 --> 00:09:49,560
No condition means the grand total.

207
00:09:49,589 --> 00:09:54,712
Step three: find the numerator
inside that row or column only.

208
00:09:54,732 --> 00:09:57,319
For or, count each person once.

209
00:09:57,339 --> 00:09:59,533
For not, use one minus.

210
00:09:59,553 --> 00:10:03,482
For an expected count, multiply
the right rate by the new total.

211
00:10:03,509 --> 00:10:06,059
Step four: check against the traps.

212
00:10:06,079 --> 00:10:09,596
Wrong choices are often the same
numerator over a different total,

213
00:10:09,616 --> 00:10:11,131
or the reverse condition.

214
00:10:11,151 --> 00:10:14,151
If there's no table, build
one with one hundred.

215
00:10:14,197 --> 00:10:14,677
Quick recap.

216
00:10:14,697 --> 00:10:17,141
Probability is favorable over total.

217
00:10:17,161 --> 00:10:19,642
Given restricts you to one row or column,

218
00:10:19,662 --> 00:10:21,713
and that total is the denominator.

219
00:10:21,733 --> 00:10:22,999
And is one cell.

220
00:10:23,019 --> 00:10:25,176
Or means count each person once.

221
00:10:25,196 --> 00:10:26,856
Not means one minus.

222
00:10:26,876 --> 00:10:29,828
Expected count is
probability times the total.

223
00:10:29,848 --> 00:10:34,971
Every question here was written for this
video in the style of the real test,

224
00:10:34,991 --> 00:10:38,114
and every table used made-up numbers.

225
00:10:38,134 --> 00:10:42,257
For official practice, the College Board's
free Question Bank lets you filter by

226
00:10:42,277 --> 00:10:46,007
skill, including probability
and conditional probability.

227
00:10:46,027 --> 00:10:47,741
If this helped, subscribe.

228
00:10:47,956 --> 00:10:51,436
The next video is SAT area and volume:

229
00:10:51,456 --> 00:10:56,777
what the reference sheet gives you, and
how the SAT makes those formulas harder.
